1502
01:07:00.740 --> 01:07:04.980
Well, Michael had a green one that had like a dollar symbol on it.

1503
01:07:05.080 --> 01:07:05.320
Remember?

1504
01:07:05.460 --> 01:07:05.580
Yep.

1505
01:07:05.580 --> 01:07:06.140
We looked it up.

1506
01:07:06.320 --> 01:07:06.600
Yep.

1507
01:07:06.740 --> 01:07:07.020
Mm-hmm.

1508
01:07:07.140 --> 01:07:10.420
And of course, he's got a jumbo set of clacky balls.

1509
01:07:10.780 --> 01:07:16.300
And he also has like a, it looks like a version of some kind of bobblehead, but I can't see

1510
01:07:16.300 --> 01:07:16.940
who it is.

1511
01:07:17.080 --> 01:07:18.100
Could you make out who it was?

1512
01:07:18.220 --> 01:07:19.580
I couldn't make out who it was.

1513
01:07:19.740 --> 01:07:22.000
If anyone knows who that is, will you let us know?

1514
01:07:22.600 --> 01:07:27.180
There's something that Mark is going to do that Michael never did, and that is play his

1515
01:07:27.180 --> 01:07:28.080
guitar for her.

1516
01:07:28.540 --> 01:07:28.880
Yeah.

1517
01:07:29.260 --> 01:07:33.280
He's going to make up a song about her while reading her resume.

1518
01:07:33.620 --> 01:07:35.040
I thought we should hear it.

1519
01:07:35.420 --> 01:07:36.220
Oh, please.

1520
01:07:37.740 --> 01:07:39.680
What if Bob Dylan was your boss?

1521
01:07:40.780 --> 01:07:41.800
I'm going to do Dylan.

1522
01:07:45.780 --> 01:07:48.000
Pam Halpert is my name.

1523
01:07:48.340 --> 01:07:53.340
I've been at Dunder Mifflin for seven years, eight years.

1524
01:07:53.600 --> 01:07:54.680
Eight years, man.

1525
01:07:55.740 --> 01:07:57.320
Got the Dunder Mifflin blues.

1526
01:07:58.000 --> 01:07:59.300
Got the Pam Halpert blues.

1527
01:07:59.940 --> 01:08:01.660
Got Pratt with the Pratt Institute.

1528
01:08:02.240 --> 01:08:03.280
You have children?

1529
01:08:03.700 --> 01:08:04.760
Two children, yes.

1530
01:08:04.760 --> 01:08:05.960
You're art and painting?

1531
01:08:06.220 --> 01:08:06.660
Mm-hmm.

1532
01:08:06.820 --> 01:08:07.740
Kind of the same thing.

1533
01:08:07.900 --> 01:08:08.800
Kind of the same thing.

1534
01:08:09.740 --> 01:08:14.380
Sometimes I repeat myself, but that's just being Pam.

1535
01:08:16.340 --> 01:08:20.000
Well, I'm kind of cute, and I'm...

1536
01:08:20.000 --> 01:08:24.180
But I'm married, so leave that be.

1537
01:08:27.420 --> 01:08:30.500
Angela, that whole thing was improvised.

1538
01:08:30.720 --> 01:08:33.160
That was a nod to David Brent.

1539
01:08:33.640 --> 01:08:38.920
When Bob and I met to practice our audition together, he did that.

1540
01:08:39.600 --> 01:08:45.900
And then when we went in to do the test audition, he brought his guitar, and we did that bit

1541
01:08:45.900 --> 01:08:49.540
as part of the test process, because David Brent...

1542
01:08:49.540 --> 01:08:50.889
In the original B.B.C.

1543
01:08:50.889 --> 01:08:51.380
version.

1544
01:08:51.740 --> 01:08:52.360
That's right.

1545
01:08:52.540 --> 01:08:53.600
He would play the guitar.

1546
01:08:54.240 --> 01:08:56.520
And so Bob did that.

1547
01:08:56.820 --> 01:09:01.160
And I remember when we were talking about bringing Bob on to play Mark, I said,

1548
01:09:01.240 --> 01:09:02.980
Greg, he's got to bring his guitar.

1549
01:09:03.840 --> 01:09:09.160
That was, like, one of my favorite audition moments was getting to sit there and just

1550
01:09:09.160 --> 01:09:11.680
react to Bob singing to me.

1551
01:09:12.360 --> 01:09:13.560
It's so funny.

1552
01:09:13.800 --> 01:09:16.940
And he finds so many hills and valleys in the moment.

1553
01:09:17.200 --> 01:09:19.980
I love when he was like, that's just being Pam.

1554
01:09:20.300 --> 01:09:20.520
Yeah.

1555
01:09:20.660 --> 01:09:23.140
But then he's like, she's pretty cute, but she's married.

1556
01:09:23.260 --> 01:09:24.700
And then to himself, he's like, leave it be.

1557
01:09:25.020 --> 01:09:25.420
Yes.

1558
01:09:25.620 --> 01:09:26.000
Yes.

1559
01:09:26.320 --> 01:09:27.340
It's so good.

1560
